I've had a number of amusing (and usually lethal) interactions with various
altars, etc.  over time.
   The funniest was the Elf who managed to kill the priest of Aerdrie Faenya.
Knowing that sacrificing an elf corpse would convert an altar, he figured that
sacrificing the priest would -really- get Aerdrie riled.  Wrong!  He was
confirmed in his new alignment, can ya believe it?  And I thought he was being
pretty chaotic...  Naturally, he went back to the Chaotic altar and started
sacrificing.  Well!  The gods BOTH got angrier and angrier, and he was dodging
lightning bolts and all kinds of nasty things until! a wide-angle disintegrate.
   Well, a wizard knew better.  He has been thoroughly and appropriately
neutral throughout.  Well, yes, so he tossed wands of fire at the angry guards,
then stood between them and the shopkeepers so as to do them in,
donating all the money to the priest till it was time for the priest to die...
then the careful manipulation to force a unicorn to walk under a stone trap
over and over until he got his gems back... finally the ring of conflict to
eliminate ALL the apprentices AND the master in the tower of wizardry!  Over
time he has prayed and blessed and accumulated so many nifty named weapons he
doesn't know what to do with 'em all, and gotten so many auras around him that
he has no idea what they're for...
   The gods smile upon a hypocrite and curse an honest man!
   Just like real life, eh?

P.S.  Is it my imagination, or is there only ONE way to get experience in this
game?  Admittedly, far more pleasant for your character than fighting, but,
is it really proper for my character to be level 30, and never gotten below
the altar in the Gnomish Mines, just because he has a taste for poontang?
(Also, is there any way for your character to become bisexual?  It would be a
major advantage!)


